 <script defer="" src="/static/help_links.js?v=1.34.19-ui41"></script><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" name="viewport"/><title>Wavelink 1.34.19 — Start here and workflow guide</title><meta content="Learn to manage checklists, operational logs and shared project records in Wavelink." name="description"/><link href="/static/icon.ico?v=1.34.19-ui31" rel="icon"/><link href="/static/help.css?v=1.34.19" rel="stylesheet"/></head><body><aside class="notice" id="historical-reference-notice">Historical reference for earlier releases and native tools. Current browser instructions are in the Help centre; earlier claims about unavailable features or administrator-only builders do not describe the current workspace.<a href="/help" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"> Open current Help</a></aside><header class="masthead"><div class="wrap"><div class="brand"><img alt="Wavelink by AJ Offshore Solutions" src="/static/wavelink-mark.svg?v=1.34.19-ui31"/><span>WAVELINK / AJ OFFSHORE SOLUTIONS</span></div><h1>Your team. Your work.<br/>One shared workspace.</h1><p class="lead">A practical guide to checklists, logs, inventory, toolbox talks and shared project records.</p><p class="release-note">1.34.19 — focused Task sections and contextual actions. Existing inventory, shipment and operational workflows remain.</p><span class="pill">USER GUIDE · VERSION 1.34.19</span><p><a href="/help/topics/companybranding" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Company branding and report customisation</a></p><div class="actions"><a href="#start">Começar</a><a href="/help/manual.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">User guide PDF</a><a href="mailto:support@mywavelink.com">Entrar em contato com o suporte</a></div></div></header><main class="wrap layout"><nav aria-label="Guide contents" class="nav"><a href="#task-details">Focused Task details</a><a href="/help/topics/qshe" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HSE / QSHE — safety and quality</a><a href="/help/topics/faults" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Fault Reports — report through closure</a><a href="#generaltasks">Tarefas gerais</a><h2>In this guide</h2><a href="#start">01  Get started</a><a href="#navigation">02  Find your workspace</a><a href="#savestatus">Conexão e salvamentos</a><a href="#network">03  Choose the hub network address</a><a href="#dashboard">04  Use the Operations dashboard</a><a href="#projects">05  Choose and manage projects</a><a href="#storage">06  Choose application and data folders</a><a href="#users">07  Manage user accounts</a><a href="#daily">08  Complete a checklist</a><a href="#builder">09  Build a checklist step by step</a><a href="#create">10  Build a checklist type</a><a href="#document">11  Checklist document details</a><a href="#originals">12  Keep and link original documents</a><a href="#illustrations">13  Add introductions and pictures</a><a href="#evidence">14  Record photographic evidence</a><a href="#evidencereview">15  Review and keep photo evidence</a><a href="#documentimport">16  Import a prepared work instruction</a><a href="#types">17  Organise and delete types</a><a href="#departments">18  Manage departments</a><a href="#approvals">19  Set up item approval</a><a href="#live">20  Use an optional live checklist</a><a href="#records">21  Manage checklist records</a><a href="#transfers">22  Export and import project workspaces</a><a href="#phones">23  Phone access and installation</a><a href="#https">24  Secure connections</a><a href="#backups">25  Back up and update</a><a href="#uninstall">26  Uninstall Wavelink</a><a href="#inventory">27  Find and move inventory</a><a href="#inventorybuilder">28  Build an inventory</a><a href="#stocktake">29  Stock verification</a><a href="#inventorytransfer">30  Import and export inventory</a><a href="#toolbox">31  Conduct a toolbox talk</a><a href="#toolboxbuilder">32  Build and import toolbox forms</a><a href="#toolboxguests">33  Add guests and collect acknowledgements</a><a href="#support">34  Help and support</a><a href="#logs">35  Create and use logbooks</a><a href="#logimport">36  Import a multi-tab operations workbook</a><a href="#logreferences">37  Review equipment and illustrated references</a><a href="#logexports">38  Export and transfer logbooks</a><a href="#offsets">39  Record lever arms and angular offsets</a><a href="#permissions">40  Set user permissions</a><a href="#logbuilder">41  Build a logbook step by step</a><a href="#assignments">42  Assign issues and follow alerts</a><a href="#datetime">43  Choose dates and times</a><a href="#tasks">44  Assign private verification tasks</a><a href="#departmentheads">45  Designate department heads</a><a href="#maintenance">46  Record maintenance work</a><a href="#maintenancebuilder">47  Build a maintenance routine</a><a href="#containers">48  Keep items inside boxes and kits</a><a href="#logwindows">49  Expand a log and keep another window open</a><a href="#certificates">50  Keep certificates with equipment</a><a href="#assetdetails">51  Open asset details and photographs</a><a href="#assetlabels">52  Print and scan inventory QR labels</a><a href="#assetcalendar">53  Use the linked project calendar</a><a href="#lowstock">54  Set low-stock alerts</a><a href="#qrverification">55  Scan labels during stock verification</a><a href="#fleet">56  Manage vessels and shore bases</a><a href="#fleetaccess">57  Set vessel-only access</a><a href="#manifests">58  Dispatch and receive with manifests</a><a href="#receiving">59  Receive equipment and record final placement</a><a href="#itemjourney">60  Follow an item’s journey</a><a href="#vessellogs">61  Use vessel-specific logbooks</a><a href="#vessellogaccess">62  Set vessel log permissions</a><a href="#accessreview">Revisar acesso efetivo e backups sensíveis</a><a href="#browseradmin">Administração e navegação pelo navegador</a><a href="#browsertemplates">Criação de listas de verificação e manutenção pelo navegador</a><a href="#browsertoolbox">Criação de formulários de diálogos de segurança pelo navegador</a><a href="/help/topics/handovers" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Handovers: private drafts and revisions</a><a href="/help/topics/handovercontinuity" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Prepare handovers &amp; current recipients</a><a href="#browserlogs">Criar livros de registro no navegador</a></nav><div class="content"><section class="chapter" id="task-details"><p class="kicker">Wavelink 1.34.19 / focused Task details</p><h2>One Task. One focused section.</h2><p>Open a general Task and use Overview, Checklist, Work &amp; review, Discussion, Linked records or the authorised Manage task section. Next action opens the right section before its existing form. Inventory-verification tasks keep their scoped workflow.</p><p>Section changes do not save results, submit or approve work. Hidden steps still count. Same-task/session refresh retains temporary view choices; account/task changes reset them. Finish or cancel an open form before navigating.</p><p><b>Original files folder organisation is future work.</b> Existing source files, revisions and exact source links are unchanged. Preserve unsent work, back up and update in place; do not uninstall first or clear browser storage.</p></section><section class="chapter" id="start"><p class="kicker">Wavelink / 01</p><h2>Começar</h2><p class="subtitle">A shared workspace for your team</p><p>Wavelink brings checklists, logs, inventory and toolbox talks into one shared project workspace. One Windows PC runs the hub. Team members use that hub from their phones, tablets or other computers.</p><p>In Admin, use the scrollable grouped sidebar. Hide sidebar and Show sidebar let you choose a compact Workspace selector when needed. Read <strong>Encontre sua área de trabalho</strong> for the command locations.</p><h3>Set up the hub</h3><ol><li>Run the Wavelink installer on the Windows hub PC. Use a 64-bit Windows 10 or 11 computer and an internet connection for setup. Follow your organisation’s software approval policy.</li><li>Abrir <strong>Administração do Wavelink</strong> and choose the project. Create its first administrator if new; otherwise use your current project account.</li><li>Abrir <strong>Configurações</strong>, review the hub name and project defaults, then save. Under <strong>Usuários e acesso</strong>, add a named account for each team member.</li><li>Em <strong>Servidor e celulares</strong>, choose the team-facing PC IP, select <strong>Salvar endereço</strong>, then <strong>Iniciar servidor</strong>. Share the saved address or QR on the approved local network.</li><li>Create a practice checklist and check that sign-in, recording, synchronisation and any required approvals work before operational use.</li></ol><h3>Join an existing hub</h3><p>You do not need to install another hub. Connect to the team’s network, open the address supplied by your administrator and sign in with your own account. From the Operations dashboard, choose Checklists or Logs. Keep the hub PC running and connected while the team needs to share or synchronise work.</p><aside class="note">Each separately installed hub has its own accounts and records. To work together, everyone must connect to the same hub.</aside><h3>Your role</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Função de acesso</th><th scope="col">What it is for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Técnico</td><td>Records checks and readings. May approve assigned items, including their own checks.</td></tr><tr><td>Supervisor</td><td>Coordinates checklist completion and can manage eligible live records.</td></tr><tr><td>Administrador</td><td>Manages users, checklist types, backups and deletion/restoration.</td></tr><tr><td>Revisor atribuído</td><td>A named person or member of an approval group. Approval assignment is separate from the user’s general role.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="chapter" data-topic="navigation" id="navigation"><p class="kicker">Wavelink 1.34.10 / continuidade da área de trabalho</p><h2>Encontre sua área de trabalho</h2><p class="subtitle">One browser workspace; the familiar desktop Admin sidebar.</p><h3>Use the main sidebar</h3><p>Open Home, Checklists, Logs, Fleet &amp; vessels, Inventory, Toolbox Talks, Handovers, Tasks, Maintenance, Certificates or Calendar from the left-aligned browser sidebar. Named administrators also have Administration. The sidebar scrolls independently; it is not replaced by duplicated Home cards.</p><h3>Fleet stays in the application</h3><p>Escolher <b>Frota e embarcações</b>. Its vessel, manifest and access views appear inside the same main workspace, with the project header and sidebar retained. It uses the current valid account. Asset-custody, manifest and administration shortcuts use the same workspace. Returning to Fleet retains its selected view and filters during this page session.</p><h3>Keep open work safe</h3><p>Save or close an open Fleet form before switching workspaces. Navigation and browser Back cannot silently discard it or submit it. An expired session opens the main sign-in; an in-memory Fleet form can resume after the same account signs in. Another account cannot adopt that open form. This is <b>not an offline Fleet draft store</b>: reloading or closing the page can lose unsubmitted wording.</p><h3>Expand logs without leaving</h3><p>In a logbook, choose <b>Expandir visualização</b> to hide the surrounding sidebar and project strip in place. Your account, logbook, section and filters remain. Choose <b>Return to normal</b> or press Escape when no entry dialog is open. A separate log window is optional, not required for expansion.</p><h3>Wide screens, phones and desktop Admin</h3><p>Use Hide sidebar / Show sidebar on wide browsers, or Menu / Close on narrow windows. Desktop Admin retains its own left-aligned sidebar and explicit controls. Its deliberately selected Open browser workspace command still opens a browser; it does not transfer a native credential into a browser.</p><h3>Account, connection and boundaries</h3><p>Use Account for account actions and help. Connection &amp; saves reports saved/local/uncertain work; Fleet also reports its live connection. Current permissions are checked by the hub. New navigation does not grant access, synchronise different hubs or fix network reachability. Daily department/shift handovers, task-owned checklists and scratch readings are available. Fault Reports now adds a separate report-to-closure workflow; evidence uploads and automatic Task creation remain future extensions.</p></section><section class="chapter" data-topic="savestatus" id="savestatus"><p class="kicker">Instruções para o usuário</p><h2>Conexão e salvamentos</h2><p class="subtitle">Saiba o que é local, confirmado ou ainda incerto</p>
 <p>Abrir <strong>Conexão e salvamentos</strong> acima da área de trabalho principal no navegador ou do portal de Embarcações. Abrir esse painel, verificar a conexão com o servidor ou revisar um aviso não envia um formulário nem conclui trabalho.</p>
